{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.GaugeTheory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.GaugeTheory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CRRealisation","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MonoidalCalcVar"],"declarations":66,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_well_defined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_well_defined","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L376-L376","doc":"All sections are gauge-equivalent (from observability). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_gauge_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs_gauge_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L374-L374","doc":"`obs` is constant on gauge-equivalence classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.gaugeEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.gaugeEquiv","kind":"def","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L372-L372","doc":"Gauge equivalence relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.obs","kind":"def","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L370-L370","doc":"The observation map `obs : Γ(S) → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.StateSections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.StateSections","kind":"def","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L368-L368","doc":"Global sections `Γ(S)` of the state bundle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L366-L366","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanObservation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanObservation","kind":"structure","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L364-L376","doc":"**Archimedean observation**: concrete realisation on a CR manifold.\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:observation-archimedean}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.substrate_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.substrate_shift","kind":"def","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L360-L360","doc":"**Substrate perturbation**: the induced shift `δq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.frobenius_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.frobenius_compat","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L358-L358","doc":"**Frobenius compatibility**: `λ ∘ O = λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.morphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.morphism","kind":"def","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L356-L356","doc":"The observation morphism `O : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L352-L352","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observation","kind":"structure","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L350-L360","doc":"**Observation** as a categorical endomorphism `O : A → A`.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:observation}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.coevaluation_contract_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.coevaluation_contract_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L331-L348","doc":"**What the bridge costs, exactly.**  Two rank-2 fields have the same\ncontraction against `fh.coevaluation` precisely when their difference is\nkilled by it.  So the scalar Einstein equation determines the rank-2 one\nonly modulo that kernel, and `FrobeniusHopfData` carries no hypothesis\nmaking the kernel trivial — there is no epi condition on `coevaluation`\nanywhere in the structure.\n\nStated as the residue rather than as a claim about `fh`, because which of\nthe two holds is a property of the particular category and is not asserted\nhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_einstein_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_einstein_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L312-L329","doc":"**Bridge (unfolded form).**  The same statement with the contraction\nwritten out, so that what is recovered is visibly the pre-retype Einstein\nequation: a morphism identity `𝟙_ C ⟶ 𝟙_ C` between the gravity scalar and\nthe sum of the Einstein and stress scalars.\n\nThis is the declaration to cite for \"the scalar form was not lost\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_einstein_contracted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_einstein_contracted","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L292-L310","doc":"**Bridge (contracted form).**  Contracting the rank-2 Einstein identity\nagainst `fh.coevaluation` — the co-pairing `FrobeniusHopfData` already\ncarries, not one introduced for this purpose — gives an identity in the\nscalars `End(𝟙_C)`.\n\nDerived, not assumed: the proof rewrites by `variational_einstein` and then\nuses additivity of `MonoidalCalcVar.contract`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.frobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.frobeniusPairing","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L277-L290","doc":"**The Frobenius pairing, as an element of the field space.**  The\nevaluation `ev = μ ≫ λ` is what the snake identities\n(`FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left` / `_right`) pair against\n`fh.coevaluation` to exhibit `A` as self-dual, and its type is\n`fh.obj ⊗ fh.obj ⟶ 𝟙_ C` verbatim — a `PairingSpace`.\n\nSo the retyped Einstein and stress slots have an inhabitant supplied by the\nsubstrate itself; the rank-2 field space is not a wider type with nothing\nin it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_transport","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L247-L260","doc":"**Transport equation** (per-instance form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_yang_mills","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_yang_mills","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L235-L245","doc":"**Yang–Mills equation** (per-instance form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.variational_einstein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.variational_einstein","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L221-L233","doc":"**Einstein equation** (per-instance form).\nUse this lemma — backed by `HasCategoricalEOM` — instead of the\ndeprecated universal axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hasCategoricalEOM_of_facts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hasCategoricalEOM_of_facts","kind":"instance","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L202-L219","doc":"**Default instance from a Fact-bundled witness**: when each of\nthe three variational identities is bundled into a `Fact`\ntriple in scope (typically from a per-`(C, fh, ca, vd)`\nconstruction), the `HasCategoricalEOM` instance follows\nimmediately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.transport","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L200-L200","doc":"**Transport**: `matter = 0` (Kobayashi–Nomizu Vol I, Ch II,\nparallel transport). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.yang_mills","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.yang_mills","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L197-L197","doc":"**Yang–Mills**: `gauge = J_ψ` (Bleecker, *Gauge Theory and\nVariational Principles*, Ch VII). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.einstein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.einstein","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L194-L194","doc":"**Einstein**: `G_λ + T_q = gravity` (Wald, *General\nRelativity*, Theorem 4.3.1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalEOM.mk","kind":"ctor","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L187-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HasCategoricalEOM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HasCategoricalEOM","kind":"class","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L183-L200","doc":"**Categorical equations of motion — typeclass.**\nWitnesses the three variational identities for a specific\n`(C, fh, ca, vd)` choice, encoding the on-shell relations\nbetween action terms and external currents/tensors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.gaugeCurrent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.gaugeCurrent","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L166-L166","doc":"The gauge current density `J_ψ`.  Unchanged: it is not summed against\nthe Einstein term, so nothing forces it to move. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.stressTensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.stressTensor","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L163-L163","doc":"The stress-energy tensor `T_q = δS_matter / δg` — **rank-2**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.einsteinTensor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.einsteinTensor","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L161-L161","doc":"The Einstein tensor `G_λ = R_λ − ½ tr(R_λ) id` — **rank-2**, a pairing\non `A ⊗ A`.  Retyped 2026-09-15 (`qou-h0ou`): it was\n`(𝟙_ C) ⟶ (𝟙_ C)`, a scalar wearing a tensor's name. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalVariationalData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalVariationalData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalVariationalData","kind":"structure","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L151-L166","doc":"**Variational EOM data**: the external morphisms appearing in the\ncategorical equations of motion — the Einstein tensor, stress-energy\ntensor, and gauge current density. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.matter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.matter","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L135-L135","doc":"**Matter term**: `λ(ψ* · D_∇ ψ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.gauge","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L133-L133","doc":"**Gauge term**: `λ ∘ tr_A(F_∇ ∧_q ⋆_q F_∇)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.gravity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.gravity","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L131-L131","doc":"**Gravity term**: `tr(q · R_λ)` — **rank-2**, a pairing on `A ⊗ A`.\nRetyped 2026-09-15: it is summed against the Einstein and stress terms,\nso it must live where a rank-2 identity can be stated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.state","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The state morphism `ψ : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.connection","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The connection on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L121-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalAction","kind":"structure","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/GaugeTheory.lean#L119-L135","doc":"**Categorical action functional** `S_q[∇, λ, ψ]`.\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-action}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-action","label":"def:categorical-action","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction.unit",